{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba PROBE-V2-RESULT.md; nl -ba claude-r20.md; nl -ba CENSUS-RESULT.md | sed -n '1,40p'; tail -27 ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# The version-2 link question: gate PASS by its registered rule; two unsupported links gone, one weak link added (D703, D704)\n     2\t\n     3\tRun: `poc/data/link-census-2026-11-21/probe-v2-{1,2,3}` (each counted: complete, every job carrying the version-2 texts, equal to old-2\n     4\twith no link row; D700's ledger: $0.0309 settled for the probe, $0.0575 in all of $0.10, 103 attempts, nothing refused or overrun).\n     5\tScored by `read_census.py --v2` against `expected-links-v2.json` (written before the probe's answers): `probe-v2-pairs.md`.\n     6\t\n     7\t## By the registered rule\n     8\t- Known positive (v9 reads v14, together): right in 3 of 3; margins 0.03, 0.07, 0.13 (fragile in two).\n     9\t- W (40, the census's 38 plus the two links across periods with no bridge): no link in any draw.\n    10\t- F (a growth rate reading an earlier revenue amount with the sign together): none.\n    11\t- **Gate: PASS.** By WORDING-V2.md §3, version 2 becomes the candidate for the paid design.\n    12\t\n    13\t## Against the current wording (every pair proposed in some draw of either; \"3/3\" = proposed in all three draws)\n    14\t\n    15\t| pair | current wording (census) | version 2 | reading |\n    16\t|---|---|---|---|\n    17\t| v9 reads v14 | 3/3 (margins 0.05, 0.09, 0.03) | 3/3 (0.03, 0.07, 0.13) | kept; still fragile |\n    18\t| v17 (FY2028 growth) reads v16 (FY2027 CPU), together | 3/3 | 0/3 | **removed** (the base-effect risk) |\n    19\t| v35 (FY2028 total) reads v9 (FY2027 Data Center) | 1/3 | 0/3 | **removed** (no bridge) |\n    20\t| v21–v9 | 3/3, direction flips (v21 reads v9 twice, v9 reads v21 once) | v21 reads v9 2/3, never reversed | **no flip** |\n    21\t| v21 (FY2027 growth) reads v16 (FY2027 CPU) | 3/3 | 3/3 | kept |\n    22\t| v16 (total CPU) reads v14 (total revenue) | 3/3 | 3/3 | kept |\n    23\t| v2 (all credit support) reads v1 (AI-cloud credit support) | 2/3 | 0/3 | lost (defensible, round 17) |\n    24\t| v35 (FY2028 total) reads v14 (FY2027 total) | 2/3 | 0/3 | lost (defensible: the outlook bridges the base, round 18) |\n    25\t| **v14 (total revenue) reads v8 (stand-alone CPU)** | 0/3 (0.47, 0.46, 0.44: below the line) | **3/3 (0.53, 0.54, 0.58)** | **added**: a whole reading a part about 5% of it; the tie-break points the other way (the total carries the full-year estimate) |\n    26\t| v16 (total CPU) reads v8 (stand-alone CPU) | 0/3 | 1/3 | added once: a whole reading its part |\n    27\t\n    28\tProposals per draw: current wording 7, 8, 5; version 2 5, 5, 6.\n    29\t\n    30\t## What it shows\n    31\t- The periods clause did what it was written for: both unsupported links across periods are gone, and so is the defensible one\n    32\t  (v35 reads v14), whose bridge Jev did not credit.\n    33\t- The tie-break did not settle direction as written: it kept v9 reads v14 at the same thin margins, and it moved v14–v8 above the line\n    34\t  in the direction it should have refused. A whole reading a part a twentieth its size gives the total little; it also makes v14 a\n    35\t  reader, so in a paid run the total's own judgements change and the Data Center question reads a changed total.\n    36\t- Stability improved where the census flipped (v21–v9), not where it was thin (v9–v14).\n     1\t# Claude's own read of the version-2 probe before Codex round 20 (written before reading codex-r20.md)\n     2\t\n     3\t- PASS as registered: version 2 is the candidate by WORDING-V2.md §3. Scored as written.\n     4\t- Net change against the current wording: two unsupported links across periods removed (the base-effect risk among them) and the one\n     5\t  flip gone; two defensible links lost (v2 reads v1, v35 reads v14); one weak link added in 3 of 3 (v14 reads v8, total revenue\n     6\t  reading a part about a twentieth of it, against the tie-break's own direction) and one once (v16 reads v8). The known positive is as\n     7\t  thin as before.\n     8\t- v14 reads v8 is weak, not harmful by its sign (more CPU revenue makes more total revenue more likely), but it makes the total a\n     9\t  reader; in the paid run v14's judgements would change and v9 would read a changed v14.\n    10\t- My lean: take version 2 as the candidate and stop tuning the wording on these 105 pairs (a third wording chosen on the same pairs is\n    11\t  selection on the probe set, AGENTS §7.3 and the council-loop traps); build it as a product version (its own question version and\n    12\t  pins, reviewed), then design the paid run with the round-13 points and ask Alex for its ceiling. Against: the paid run would then\n    13\t  carry v14 as a reader, which muddies the Data Center comparison; a run that measures v9 against an unchanged v14 needs the July\n    14\t  shape's controls or a decision to hold v14's links out of the reading.\n     1\t# The census of link decisions over the window: gate PASS by the registered rule; direction unsettled (D700, D701; 2026-11-21)\n     2\t\n     3\tRun: `poc/data/link-census-2026-11-21/` (three draws, each counted: complete, both July seq-148 answers reused, equal to old-2 with no\n     4\tlink row; one ledger at Alex's $0.10: settled $0.0266 at the ledger's rule of three times each reported input, 52 attempts, nothing\n     5\trefused or overrun). Scored by `read_census.py` against `expected-links.json` (written before any census answer; R 1, W 38, O 66):\n     6\t`census-pairs.md` (every pair and draw).\n     7\t\n     8\t## By the registered rule\n     9\t- **Known positive (v9 Data Center FY2027 reads v14 total revenue FY2027, together):** right in 3 of 3 draws; margins 0.05, 0.09,\n    10\t  0.03 (the July samples, fragile).\n    11\t- **W pairs (38, the shown material names no connection):** no link in any draw. Wrong links: 0.\n    12\t- **Gate: PASS.**\n    13\t\n    14\t## The O pairs that were linked (reported, not scored)\n    15\t\n    16\t| seq | pair | draw 1 | draw 2 | draw 3 | reading |\n    17\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n    18\t| 8 | v2 (all credit support, guarantees, backstops) – v1 (AI-cloud credit support) | v2 reads v1, 0.58 | v2 reads v1, 0.51 | no link (0.48) | a whole reads its part; 2 of 3 |\n    19\t| 265 | v16 (total CPU FY2027) – v14 (total revenue FY2027) | v16 reads v14, 0.82 | 0.82 | 0.83 | a part reads its whole; stable |\n    20\t| 321 | v17 (total revenue growth FY2028) – v16 (total CPU FY2027) | v17 reads v16, 0.50 | 0.50 | 0.55 | a company-wide figure reads a part of the year before; at the line |\n    21\t| 534 | v21 (total revenue growth FY2027) – v16 (total CPU FY2027) | v21 reads v16, 0.73 | 0.72 | 0.76 | a whole reads its part; stable |\n    22\t| 534 | v21 – v9 (Data Center FY2027) | v21 reads v9, 0.53 | **v9 reads v21**, 0.52 | v21 reads v9, 0.60 | the direction flips between draws |\n    23\t| 1238 | v35 (total revenue FY2028) – v14 (total revenue FY2027) | v35 reads v14, 0.52 | 0.54 | no link (0.44) | another period of the same quantity; 2 of 3 |\n    24\t| 1238 | v35 – v9 | no link | v35 reads v9, 0.50 | no link | 1 of 3 |\n    25\t\n    26\tEvery proposed link carried the sign together. Proposals per draw: 7, 8, 5 (proposals: the census writes no link).\n    27\t\n    28\t## What it shows\n    29\t- **No link between unrelated questions.** Across 3 × 38 W decisions, Jev never linked a financing amount to a revenue or margin\n    30\t  question, or two financing amounts of different kinds.\n    31\t- **The direction of a part against its whole is not settled by the criterion.** The same version reads part-to-whole (v9 → v14,\n    32\t  v16 → v14) and whole-to-part (v2 → v1, v21 → v16, v21 → v9), and one pair flips between draws (v21–v9). This is the class §3 named\n    33\t  (\"abstract\": the criterion's two clauses admit both directions), now counted on the whole window: of the 8 pairs linked in some draw,\n    34\t  4 take the same direction in 3 of 3 draws (v9 → v14, v16 → v14, v17 → v16, v21 → v16), 3 are linked in only 1 or 2 draws, and 1\n    35\t  flips direction.\n    36\t- **Fragile decisions:** 6 of the linked or required decisions sit within 0.10 of the next class (v9 → v14 in all three; v17 → v16 in\n    37\t  two; v21–v9 in one).\n    38\t\n    39\t## What it means for the paid run\n    40\t- A linked sequence of the paid run can take its link answers from its paired census draw: a link request depends on the candidate's\n\n## D703 · 2026-11-21 · Alex chooses to probe a sharpened link question before the paid run\n\n- **The question** (after D702): \"连题统计通过了事先定的关 … 问题是它在'部分读整体'和'整体读部分'之间拿不定主意，而且有一条很可能连反了 … 下一步怎么走？\"\n  Options: 先试新问法 (recommended: with Codex at $0, write the link question clearly, keeping Data Center reads total revenue and the\n  38 negatives, removing unsupported links including the base effect, no blanket ban on a whole reading its part; then ask the same\n  105 pairs three times, about 3 cents, from the 7 cents left of the approved 10; then decide the paid run); 直接正式运行 (the current\n  wording, about $7 estimated, ceiling later); 停在这里 (poc-v118 stays, the linking version paused).\n- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-21): \"先试新问法 (推荐)\".\n- **Decided (Alex):** a sharpened READS/SIGN wording is designed with the council at $0 and probed on the same 105 pairs, three draws,\n  within the remaining $0.073 of D700's ledger. Then the paid run is decided.\n\n## D704 · 2026-11-21 · Council R passes the version-2 link question for its probe (rounds 18–19); the probe is sent under D703\n\n- **The wording** (`docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/WORDING-V2.md`, harness-only, no product file changed): a tie-break (when\n  either question could read the other, the one less anchored by guidance, consensus or a reported figure for the quantity and full\n  period it asks about reads the other; no direction banned); a periods clause (quantities of different periods are linked only when\n  the supplied text states how one moves the other); a base-effect SIGN example. The tie-break and the periods clause are proposals\n  this probe tests under D703; D537 decided only the Data Center case.\n- **The council:** round 18 NOT READY (the gate could pass while keeping an unsupported cross-period link; the tie-break's period and\n  the periods example needed precision); round 19 READY FOR THE V2 PROBE. Registration for version 2, written before its answers: R 1,\n  W 40 (the census's 38 plus 321:v16 and 1238:v9, no bridge across periods), O 61, F 3 (a growth rate reading an earlier revenue amount\n  with the sign together). $0: the dry pass complete and equal to old-2 with every job carrying the version-2 texts; its mutant (texts\n  not patched) stops before any send; the stored census answers fail the version-2 gate, the round-18 counterexample fails it, a\n  control with both unsupported links removed passes.\n- **Sent:** `window_test.py probe-v2`, draws 1, 2, 3 one after another on D700's ledger ($0.0734 left); a ceiling stop before draw 3\n  is an incomplete probe with no verdict.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba DESIGN.md | sed -n '136,204p'; rg -n 'def _dependency_lines_full|def topological|def queued_by_change|def round|current_state' ../../../src/hivemind/views/judging.py; nl -ba WORDING-V2.md | sed -n '15,65p'; rg -n 'retire|fresh' ../2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba DESIGN.md | sed -n '136,204p'; rg -n 'def _dependency_lines_full|def topological|def queued_by_change|def round|current_state' ../../../src/hivemind/views/judging.py; nl -ba WORDING-V2.md | sed -n '15,65p'; rg -n 'retire|fresh' ../2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md\"","aggregated_output":"   136\tthree refusals are artefacts of reading the final state (v28 and v14 \"already have a successor\", v40 \"closed\": the successions and the\n   137\tclosing came later); the 10 skipped are D197 shared-quantity records the preflight lookup cannot identify (round 15); enum names 46, none missing; 42 keyed open views, no\n   138\tduplicate key. The `neither` pass, which replays every request with the state of its time, met every request in the archive.\n   139\t\n   140\t## 4. The paid run (after the census, the council and Alex's ceiling)\n   141\t\n   142\t- **Linked, three sequences:** poc-v119, each on its own copy of old-2's archive and an empty ledger, the whole window. Jev's link\n   143\t  answers are not byte-stable (the July probabilities moved by up to 0.03), so the three may choose different links; each is read.\n   144\t- **Control, three sequences:** poc-v118 on its own archive copy with the judge rows of every reader of the linked sequences (their\n   145\t  union) retired from the seq of that reader's first link, so their judgements are fresh samples of the same requests old-2 sent.\n   146\t- **old-2's stored path** is a fourth control path, labelled: v9's self-made reference was found on it, so it is not a neutral draw.\n   147\t- Order: the three linked sequences first (they decide the readers), then the three controls. One shared reservation ledger under the\n   148\t  ceiling Alex names; a refused reservation or a stop makes the comparison inconclusive.\n   149\t- Each sequence uses the comparison runs' budget transport with July's settlement (cache writes at 1.25x), and an allow-list before\n   150\t  it: a sequence may buy only link questions and the judgements of its readers (linked) or of the retired readers (control); any other\n   151\t  request that misses the archive stops that sequence (July's latch).\n   152\t\n   153\tRound 13's points for the paid design's own round (not built yet): pair each control with its linked sequence and retire that\n   154\treader's original and retry requests from its first affected judgement, not the union; keep old-2 a labelled baseline outside the\n   155\tfresh-control mean; run the fresh calls together; report linked-only judgement days apart; record link choices that differ from the\n   156\tcensus.\n   157\t\n   158\t## 5. Reading rule (to be frozen before the paid send)\n   159\t\n   160\tRound 13's points, to be taken into this rule before its own round: part–whole contradiction only on matching scope and period, a\n   161\tdefinite contradiction kept apart from overlapping ranges, a remainder floor only where the evidence establishes it; a sign gives no\n   162\tbound; a self-made reference traced to an outside statement of the right scope (the text scan clears a figure copied from the linked\n   163\tforecast); July's arithmetic-and-assumption check kept; rates on common question-pair dates, the three whole trajectories as the\n   164\tindependent repeats, pass, fail and inconclusive defined for zero links and too few dates, and the halving rule checked control\n   165\tagainst control.\n   166\t\n   167\tPer linked pair (reader R reads T), over every day R is judged; scored by Claude first, then by a blind reader under shuffled labels.\n   168\t- **A, the links:** each link committed in a linked sequence, read with both questions and ladders: right or wrong (relation,\n   169\t  direction, sign).\n   170\t- **B, contradiction:** for a part read against its whole, R's implied outcome above T's implied outcome, or leaving less for the rest\n   171\t  than the reported rest of the latest quarter carried over the remaining quarters (July's rule C generalised); for another relation,\n   172\t  R's implied outcome on the side of its ladder that T's conclusion and the sign rule out, stated as such in the reasons.\n   173\t- **C, self-made reference:** `self-reference/reference_census.py`'s three measures on every reader judgement, linked against controls.\n   174\t- **D, harm:** a reader calling T's forecast a market figure or evidence (grounding error); first-attempt refusals; failed articles;\n   175\t  any judgement outside the reading chains differing from old-2's (code).\n   176\t- **Pass line (proposed, for the council):** every committed link right by both readers; B: linked days in contradiction at most half\n   177\t  the controls' mean, with the controls showing at least two (else \"not tested\"); C: linked at most the controls' mean; D: no\n   178\t  grounding error and no failed article in the linked arm, refusals at most the controls' plus two, every other judgement equal to\n   179\t  old-2's.\n   180\t\n   181\t## 6. Cost (estimate, to be priced from the census)\n   182\t\n   183\tLink questions: Jev input at $0.042 per million tokens, July's two jobs cost under $0.001. Reader judgements: old-2's stored v9\n   184\tjudgements cost about $0.003 each at published rates (July's `price`); a reader judged about 70 times over the window, plus the days a\n   185\tchanged T queues it. Priced from the census's readers and old-2's stored judgement tokens before the ceiling question.\n   186\t\n   187\t## 7. State × event (the harness; the product path's rows are DESIGN.md §6 of the dependency design)\n   188\t\n   189\t| Event | Outcome |\n   190\t|---|---|\n   191\t| a request outside the allow-list misses the archive | the sequence stops (latch), final, reported; the comparison is inconclusive if any sequence stops |\n   192\t| a request old-2's run refused | its stored answer is given back once; the check refuses it again; the stored retry follows |\n   193\t| a fresh reader answer is refused twice | the article or the day fails as in the product; the sequence stops; reported |\n   194\t| a link closes a circle | one correction per link (product path); a persistent circle fails the article: the sequence stops |\n   195\t| a reservation would pass the ceiling | refused, the ledger stops, every sequence stops: inconclusive |\n   196\t| a process dies | the sequence is final (never resumed); the reservation stays counted |\n   197\t| two sequences at once | separate folders and archive copies; one shared ledger under its lock |\n   198\t\n   199\t## 8. Prior decisions\n   200\t\n   201\tD694 (A), D695 (number questions only), D696 (reservation from request size), D697/D698 (the July proof and result), D699 (A for the\n   202\twhole window), D537 (part reads whole) and PRD 06 line 134 (D368/D208: root reads drivers), D677 (no paid work unless Alex funds a run\n   203\twith a written path to passing: D699 is that funding; this document is the path), D667 (three draws for totals; D431's same-day rule\n   204\tdoes not apply: every sequence reads the same stored articles), D449 (a crash stops the run).\n82:    last = store.current_state(conn, view_id)\n86:        state = store.current_state(conn, theme_id)\n103:def topological(conn, view_ids):\n127:def _dependency_lines_full(conn, target, d, state, rung_label, tv, flag):\n162:            state = store.current_state(conn, target)\n192:    last = store.current_state(conn, view_id)\n247:    last = store.current_state(conn, view_id)\n287:def queued_by_change(conn, view_id):\n305:def round_of_judgements(archive, cfg, conn, changed_views, seq, item, *, transport=None):\n    15\t\n    16\tREADS, `candidate_reads_thesis`, appended sentence:\n    17\t> When either question could be judged with the other in view, the one whose answer the supplied text anchors less (no guidance,\n    18\t> consensus or reported figure for the quantity and full period the question asks about) is the one judged with the other's conclusion\n    19\t> in view.\n    20\t\n    21\tREADS, `neither`, appended clause (before \"sharing a company ...\"):\n    22\t> or quantities of different periods when the supplied text does not state how one period's answer moves the other's (a retailer's\n    23\t> sales this year and its sales growth next year, when the text only names both)\n    24\t\n    25\tSIGN, `opposite`, added example:\n    26\t> ...; one year's sales and the next year's sales growth at a given next-year level, since a higher base lowers the growth\n    27\t\n    28\t`thesis_reads_candidate` (\"for the same reasons with the roles swapped\") and the instructions are unchanged, so the tie-break applies\n    29\tboth ways: a part with guidance and a whole without would have the whole read the part. No direction is banned.\n    30\t\n    31\tSources (round 18 made the distinction explicit): the general tie-break and the periods clause are proposals this probe is authorized\n    32\tto test by D703, not rules already decided; D537 decided only the concrete case (Data Center revenue reading total revenue, the total\n    33\tcarrying the year's consensus), and D260 explains why guidance and consensus anchor a judgement (it governs judging, not linking). The\n    34\tbase-effect example is the arithmetic of a growth rate with the next-year level held fixed. The periods clause narrows the dependency\n    35\tdesign §2 (\"another period of the same quantity may be linked\") to \"when the supplied text states how\": a link across periods still\n    36\texists when the text gives the bridge (v35 reads v14: the FY2028 outlook translates growth into a level through the FY2027 base).\n    37\tRound 18 read the seq-148 request (dry archive, call 8744): the total carries Bloomberg's $393B FY2027 estimate, Data Center a Q1\n    38\tfigure of $75.25B (92% of the quarter): a full-year anchor against a partial-year one, so the tie-break gives v9 reads v14. Growth: 595\n    39\tcharacters across the three criteria texts (READS `candidate_reads_thesis` +269, `neither` +209, SIGN `opposite` +117; the READS\n    40\tcriteria repeat in every pair of a job, about 120 tokens a pair); written reason: the audit shows a missing case and an abstract clause, and nothing in the current texts\n    41\tduplicates them to cut.\n    42\t\n    43\t## 3. What the probe decides (registered before its answers: `expected-links-v2.json`)\n    44\t\n    45\tThe census's registration (R 1, W 38, O 66) with, for version 2 only (`expected-links-v2.json`): **W** for any link across periods\n    46\twhose shown text gives no bridge, the two unsupported links council R named (321:v16, v17 FY2028 growth against v16 FY2027 CPU; 1238:v9,\n    47\tv35 FY2028 total against v9 FY2027 Data Center; round 18 showed the gate passing without this); **F**, the base-effect sign, a growth\n    48\trate reading an earlier period's revenue amount with the sign together (321:v8, 321:v9, 321:v14). Version 2: R 1, W 40, O 61, F 3;\n    49\t1238:v14 stays O and is reported. Gate: the known positive right in 3 of 3 draws, no W link, no F link. $0 checks on the stored census\n    50\tanswers (`scorer-checks.log`): as stored, FAIL on 321:v16 and 1238:v9; with 321:v16 made \"neither\" and 1238:v9 kept, FAIL; with both\n    51\tmade \"neither\", PASS; 321:v16 linked with the sign opposite, FAIL; 321:v14 linked together, FAIL. Reported beside: every O pair\n    52\tagainst the census, and the margins.\n    53\t- **Pass:** version 2 becomes the candidate for the paid design (a product version built and reviewed first).\n    54\t- **Fail on the known positive or a W link:** the current wording stays the candidate with its measured risks (D702).\n    55\t- **Fail on F only:** the base-effect sentence did not take; reported, the current wording's risk stands.\n    56\t- **A ceiling stop before draw 3 completes:** an incomplete probe, no verdict (round 18: the observed job shapes price at about $0.034\n    57\t  for three draws; the all-SIGN stress shape at 0.37 tokens a byte at about $0.074 against $0.0734 left).\n    58\t\n    59\t## 4. The probe\n    60\t\n    61\t`window_test.py probe-v2 <scratch> <draw> <ledger> 0.10`: the census pass with the version-2 texts patched into `links.READS` and\n    62\t`links.SIGN` for the pass; every link job is new (the July answers do not match the new texts), so the seq-148 jobs are bought. Three\n    63\tdraws on D700's ledger (spent $0.0266, $0.0734 left); priced as the census (a draw settles about $0.009 at the ledger's rule; the READS\n    64\trequests grow by about 120 tokens a pair). The completeness check, equality with old-2 and the paid-transport record apply as in the\n    65\tcensus; `draw.json` records the wording.\n16:   row for v9 or v14 (request user text beginning \"Thesis v9 (\" or \"Thesis v14 (\") is retired by the existing `Archive.retire`\n19:   retired and is not returned again.\n37:**Archive per sequence:** its own writable copy of old-2's archive with the v9 and v14 judge rows retired (step 2 above), so both\n38:questions are judged fresh every day (council R round 3) and every other request replays by exact identity. The harness holds\n47:that every v9 and v14 judgement of 07-10..07-12 was answered by a provider attempt of its own sequence (fresh), never by the archive.\n84:- **Readers:** Claude's marks written first, then a fresh blind Codex reader on the six sequences under shuffled labels, the key outside\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
