pair shown\": [\n    14\t  {\n    15\t   \"attempt\": \"gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45#1\",\n    16\t   \"seq\": 8,\n174:   \"proposed\": [],\n262:     \"stage\": \"reads\",\n266:   \"proposed\": [],\n280:   \"proposed\": [],\n294:   \"proposed\": [],\n308:   \"proposed\": [],\n322:   \"proposed\": [],\n327:   \"seq\": 148,\n466:     \"stage\": \"reads\",\n477:     \"stage\": \"sign\",\n     1\t{\n     2\t \"equal to old-2\": true,\n     3\t \"link jobs asked\": 17,\n     4\t \"questions in them\": 112,\n     5\t \"old-2's refused answers met again\": [\n     6\t  \"cfd45dde68ce\",\n     7\t  \"907eb29065b7\",\n     8\t  \"6d0c31a8460d\",\n     9\t  \"137e5f747345\"\n    10\t ],\n    11\t \"left unmet\": [],\n    12\t \"link rows written\": 0,\n    13\t \"openings with a pair shown\": [\n    14\t  {\n    15\t   \"attempt\": \"gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45#1\",\n    16\t   \"seq\": 8,\n174:   \"proposed\": [],\n262:     \"stage\": \"reads\",\n266:   \"proposed\": [],\n280:   \"proposed\": [],\n294:   \"proposed\": [],\n308:   \"proposed\": [],\n322:   \"proposed\": [],\n327:   \"seq\": 148,\n466:     \"stage\": \"reads\",\n477:     \"stage\": \"sign\",\n     1\t{\n     2\t \"equal to old-2\": true,\n     3\t \"link jobs asked\": 17,\n     4\t \"questions in them\": 112,\n     5\t \"old-2's refused answers met again\": [\n     6\t  \"cfd45dde68ce\",\n     7\t  \"907eb29065b7\",\n     8\t  \"6d0c31a8460d\",\n     9\t  \"137e5f747345\"\n    10\t ],\n    11\t \"left unmet\": [],\n    12\t \"link rows written\": 0,\n    13\t \"openings with a pair shown\": [\n    14\t  {\n    15\t   \"attempt\": \"gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45#1\",\n    16\t   \"seq\": 8,\n174:   \"proposed\": [],\n262:     \"stage\": \"reads\",\n266:   \"proposed\": [],\n280:   \"proposed\": [],\n294:   \"proposed\": [],\n308:   \"proposed\": [],\n322:   \"proposed\": [],\n327:   \"seq\": 148,\n466:     \"stage\": \"reads\",\n477:     \"stage\": \"sign\",\n6:- **A. Comparable answers:** both 07-12 answers give a FY2027 forecast in USD for their own quantity (a range by its stated ends);\n8:- **B. Arithmetic and sources:** reported figures keep their amount and scope; the arithmetic follows from the stated inputs within\n10:  forecast is treated as a forecast with assumptions.\n11:- **C. Room for the rest:** the high end of the Data Center forecast is at least $6B below the low end of the company forecast (the Q1\n13:- **D. The link did the work (linked arm):** matching chose \"v9 reads v14\", the writer committed it at seq 148, and v9 used v14's\n14:  forecast in its calculation or as a stated bound; delivery and use of the Bloomberg-compiled $393B (e195) recorded separately; a\n17:  material grounding error on either question across 07-10..07-12 (relabelling a system forecast as a market estimate, or treating\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/views/links.py | sed -n '135,155p'; nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/views/judging.py | sed -n '242,279p'; rg -n 'def current_state|CREATE TABLE.*judgements|create table.*judgements' ../../../src/hivemind/views/store.py; nl -ba ../2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/reading-rule.md | sed -n '1,29p'; nl -ba ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '10493,10514p'; rg -n '\"'^ '\"\\\\\\\"(148:v8|148:v9)\\\\\\\"|scope' expected-links-v2.json | head\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/views/links.py | sed -n '135,155p'; nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/views/judging.py | sed -n '242,279p'; rg -n 'def current_state|CREATE TABLE.*judgements|create table.*judgements' ../../../src/hivemind/views/store.py; nl -ba ../2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/reading-rule.md | sed -n '1,29p'; nl -ba ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '10493,10514p'; rg -n '\"'^ '\"\\\\\\\"(148:v8|148:v9)\\\\\\\"|scope' expected-links-v2.json | head\"","aggregated_output":"   135\t        return oriented_like(c, store.rungs_of(conn, target), [])['rungs']\n   136\t    return c['rungs']\n   137\t\n   138\t\n   139\t# ---------- the reading graph ----------\n   140\t\n   141\tdef stored_edges(conn):\n   142\t    \"\"\"Every stored dependency at its effective target (a bound wait counts through the question it is bound to).\"\"\"\n   143\t    edges = {}\n   144\t    for (view_id,) in conn.execute('select distinct view_id from dependencies'):\n   145\t        for dep in store.dependencies_of(conn, view_id):\n   146\t            if dep['resolved_to']:\n   147\t                edges.setdefault(view_id, set()).add(dep['resolved_to'])\n   148\t    return edges\n   149\t\n   150\t\n   151\tdef unbound_waits(conn):\n   152\t    return conn.execute(\"select count(*) from dependencies where coalesce(depends_on, '')='' and coalesce(wait_year, '')!='' \"\n   153\t                        \"and dependency_id not in (select dependency_id from dependency_resolutions)\").fetchone()[0]\n   154\t\n   155\t\n   242\t        if push['evidence_id'] not in allowed:\n   243\t            errors.append(bad_push(push['evidence_id']))\n   244\t    for field in STANCE_FIELDS:\n   245\t        if not str(data.get(field) or '').strip():\n   246\t            errors.append(f'{field} is empty: state what the market expects and the figure or date the evidence implies')\n   247\t    last = store.current_state(conn, view_id)\n   248\t    if last is None and not data['changed']:\n   249\t        errors.append('first judgement must say changed')\n   250\t    if last is not None and last['rung'] != data['rung'] and not data['changed']:\n   251\t        errors.append(f'rung moved from {last[\"rung\"]} to {data[\"rung\"]} but changed is false')\n   252\t    return errors\n   253\t\n   254\t\n   255\tdef _record(conn, cfg, view_id, seq, item, answer):\n   256\t    data = vocabulary.judgement_answer(answer.data)\n   257\t    judgement_id = store.insert(conn, 'judgements', view_id=view_id, seq=seq, input_id=item['input_id'], rung=data['rung'],\n   258\t                                reasons=data['reasons'], cited_evidence_json=json.dumps(data['cites']), cited_views_json=json.dumps(data['cites_views']),\n   259\t                                pushes_json=json.dumps(data['pushes'], ensure_ascii=False), changed=1 if data['changed'] else 0,\n   260\t                                theme_pushes_json=json.dumps(data.get('theme_pushes', []), ensure_ascii=False),\n   261\t                                reference=data.get('reference'), implied_outcome=data.get('implied_outcome'),\n   262\t                                why_changed=data['why_changed'], config_checksum=cfg.checksum, call_id=answer.call_id,\n   263\t                                request_sha256=answer.request_sha256, publication_day=item['publication_day'])\n   264\t    conn.commit()\n   265\t    return {'view_id': view_id, 'judgement_id': judgement_id, 'rung': data['rung'], 'changed': data['changed'], 'cost': answer.cost_usd, 'cached': answer.cached}\n   266\t\n   267\t\n   268\tJUDGE_WORKERS = 32     # a day's round is up to 40 judgements of about 16 s each in two dependency levels (themes, then assets); 32 at a time makes a round about two calls long (2026-11-02)\n   269\t\n   270\t\n   271\tdef upstream(conn, view_id):\n   272\t    \"\"\"Every view this one depends on, directly or through its dependencies.\"\"\"\n   273\t    seen, stack = set(), [view_id]\n   274\t    while stack:\n   275\t        for dep in store.dependencies_of(conn, stack.pop()):\n   276\t            target = dep['resolved_to']\n   277\t            if target and target not in seen:\n   278\t                seen.add(target)\n   279\t                stack.append(target)\n234:def current_state(conn, view_id):\n     1\t# The July test: reading rule, frozen 2026-11-21 before any send (D694 (c))\n     2\t\n     3\tCopied from `TEST-PLAN.md` without change; scored line by line as written.\n     4\t\n     5\t## Reading rule (frozen before the send; council R round 2, `codex-r2.md` §7(b), with round 3)\n     6\t- **A. Comparable answers:** both 07-12 answers give a FY2027 forecast in USD for their own quantity (a range by its stated ends);\n     7\t  quarters recorded where both give comparable figures; a missing annual figure leaves reconciliation untested.\n     8\t- **B. Arithmetic and sources:** reported figures keep their amount and scope; the arithmetic follows from the stated inputs within\n     9\t  rounding; each assumption that materially sizes the result is disclosed and supported by the material available that day; a linked\n    10\t  forecast is treated as a forecast with assumptions.\n    11\t- **C. Room for the rest:** the high end of the Data Center forecast is at least $6B below the low end of the company forecast (the Q1\n    12\t  floor: $81.6B total minus $75.25B Data Center); each comparable quarter keeps the segment within the total.\n    13\t- **D. The link did the work (linked arm):** matching chose \"v9 reads v14\", the writer committed it at seq 148, and v9 used v14's\n    14\t  forecast in its calculation or as a stated bound; delivery and use of the Bloomberg-compiled $393B (e195) recorded separately; a\n    15\t  mention or citation alone earns no credit.\n    16\t- **Pass:** at least two of three linked sequences meet A–D; at most one control meets A–C; no first-attempt refusal added and no new\n    17\t  material grounding error on either question across 07-10..07-12 (relabelling a system forecast as a market estimate, or treating\n    18\t  $393B as a Data Center consensus, is one). **Inconclusive:** two or more controls reconcile, fewer than two comparable sequences in\n    19\t  either arm, or a ceiling stop. **Fail:** a new material error, an added refusal, fewer than two correct link selections, or any other\n    20\t  miss. Failures take precedence.\n    21\t- **Readers:** Claude's marks written first, then a fresh blind Codex reader on the six sequences under shuffled labels, the key outside\n    22\t  the repository; every sequence reported.\n 10493\t## D698 · 2026-11-21 · The July test of the linking version passes its frozen rule; next steps go to Alex\n 10494\t\n 10495\t- **Result** (`docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/JULY-RESULT.md`, $0.0689 of $0.15): in all three linked\n 10496\t  sequences the matcher chose and the writer committed \"v9 reads v14\" at seq 148 and nothing else. Linked sequences meeting A–D: 3 of 3\n 10497\t  (Claude), 2 of 3 (blind Codex reader); controls meeting A–C: 1 of 3 (Claude), 0 of 3 (reader); no refusal, no grounding error. PASS by\n 10498\t  both readers; their two disagreements (control-1's unsized uplift, linked-2's \"stated bound\") do not move it.\n 10499\t- **Disclosed with it:** the stored annual contradiction did not recur in the fresh controls (the total rose to ~$411B on 07-12); the\n 10500\t  controls' remaining contradictions are in the implied second half, which rule C cannot see; the verdict rests on B read as written\n 10501\t  for two controls; coherence is not accuracy; one pair, three days.\n 10502\t- **Open:** PRD 06 still says the default matcher is not asked for dependencies (true of poc-v118, the product); it changes with the\n 10503\t  decision that makes a linking version the product. The sourced-reference change (D693) waits for a longer linked run.\n 10504\t\n 10505\t## D699 · 2026-11-21 · Alex continues with A: the whole-window measurement of the linking version, designed with the council at $0 first\n 10506\t\n 10507\t- **Alex's words** (2026-11-21), replying to the next-step question after D698 (A, recommended: run poc-v119 over 07-01..09-20 once,\n 10508\t  about $9 as one poc-v118 run cost, its measurement designed with the council at $0 before any send: whether related number questions\n 10509\t  still contradict each other, which links the matcher chose and whether any is wrong, whether the self-made market reference becomes\n 10510\t  rarer, whether other questions get worse; then decide whether the new version replaces the product. B: stop, poc-v118 stays): \"continue\".\n 10511\t- **Decided (Alex):** A. The $0 design and its council come first. The ~$9 was an estimate, not a ceiling: the paid send waits for the\n 10512\t  council's pass and a ceiling Alex names. poc-v118 stays the product until a later decision.\n 10513\t- **Next:** the design (`docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/`), its $0 proofs, council rounds, then the ceiling question to Alex.\n 10514\t\n38: \"148:v9\": {\n44: \"148:v8\": {\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import collections as co, contextlib, io, json, math, pathlib, sqlite3\nimport read_census as rc\nimport window_test as wt\nfrom hivemind import jev, model\nfrom hivemind.views import links, store, judging\nhere=pathlib.Path.cwd()\nrepo=here.parents[2]\nroot=repo/'\\\\''poc/data/link-census-2026-11-21'\\\\''\ndef con(f): return sqlite3.connect(f.as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro&immutable=1'\\\\'',uri=True)\nledger=json.loads((root/'\\\\''ledger.json'\\\\'').read_text())\nsettled=[json.loads(l) for l in (root/'\\\\''ledger.attempts.jsonl'\\\\'').read_text().splitlines()]\nassert len(settled)==ledger['\\\\''attempts'\\\\'']==103 and all(x['\\\\''kind'\\\\'']=='\\\\''jev'\\\\'' and x['\\\\''charged'\\\\'']<=x['\\\\''reserved'\\\\''] for x in settled)\nassert math.isclose(sum(x['\\\\''charged'\\\\''] for x in settled),ledger['\\\\''spent'\\\\''])\noldcalls=settled[:52]\ntokens=[]\nbaseall=[]\nvarall=[]\nmanifest=json.loads((here/'\\\\''expected-links-v2.json'\\\\'').read_text())\ncfg=wt.config.load(str(wt.V119))\nfor version,prefix,output in [(None,'\\\\''census'\\\\'','\\\\''census-pairs.md'\\\\''),('\\\\''v2'\\\\'','\\\\''probe-v2'\\\\'','\\\\''probe-v2-pairs.md'\\\\'')]:\n dirs=[root/f'\\\\''{prefix}-{i}'\\\\'' for i in range(1,4)]\n capture=io.StringIO()\n with contextlib.redirect_stdout(capture):\n    rc.main((['\\\\''--v2'\\\\''] if version else [])+list(map(str,dirs)))\n assert capture.getvalue()==(here/output).read_text()\n print(output,'\\\\''regenerated identically'\\\\'')\n for i,folder in enumerate(dirs,1):\n    cc=json.loads((folder/'\\\\''census.json'\\\\'').read_text())\n    with con(folder/'\\\\''views.sqlite'\\\\'') as v, con(folder/'\\\\''archive.sqlite'\\\\'') as a:\n       assert cc['\\\\''equal to old-2'\\\\''] and cc['\\\\''link rows written'\\\\'']==0 and wt.complete(cc)==(True,[])\n       assert v.execute('\\\\''select count(*) from dependencies'\\\\'').fetchone()[0]==0\n       choices=rc.decisions(folder/'\\\\''views.sqlite'\\\\'')\n       got=co.Counter()\n       graph=co.defaultdict(set)\n       item_jobs=[]\n       for opening in cc['\\\\''openings with a pair shown'\\\\'']:\n          seq=opening['\\\\''seq'\\\\'']\n          for pair in opening['\\\\''pairs'\\\\'']:\n             th=pair.get('\\\\''thesis'\\\\'')\n             if '\\\\''reads'\\\\'' in pair: got['\\\\''reads'\\\\'']+=1\n             if '\\\\''sign'\\\\'' in pair: got['\\\\''sign'\\\\'']+=1\n          for j in opening['\\\\''calls'\\\\'']:\n             jid,sha=j['\\\\''call_id'\\\\''],j['\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\'']\n             sha2,req_text,reply_text,ans_text,t,created=a.execute('\\\\''select request_sha256,request_json,response_json,answer_json,input_tokens,created_at from model_calls where call_id=?'\\\\'',(jid,)).fetchone()\n             assert j['\\\\''status'\\\\'']=='\\\\''answered'\\\\'' and sha2==sha\n             req=json.loads(req_text); reply=json.loads(reply_text); ans=json.loads(ans_text)\n             assert model.request_identity(req)[1]==sha and sorted(req['\\\\''questions'\\\\''])==j['\\\\''questions'\\\\'']\n             assert jev.validate(ans,req['\\\\''questions'\\\\''])==[] and reply['\\\\''answers'\\\\'']==ans\n             if version=='\\\\''v2'\\\\'':\n                assert j['\\\\''archived_before'\\\\''] is False and reply['\\\\''usage'\\\\'']['\\\\''input_tokens'\\\\'']==t\n                tokens.append(t)\n                rs,sg=wt.wording_v2()\n                for q in req['\\\\''questions'\\\\''].values(): assert q['\\\\''criteria'\\\\'']==(rs if j['\\\\''stage'\\\\'']=='\\\\''reads'\\\\'' else sg)\n                if seq==148:\n                   print(prefix,i,'\\\\''July'\\\\'',j['\\\\''stage'\\\\''],jid,sha[:12],created,t)\n                   if i==1 and j['\\\\''stage'\\\\'']=='\\\\''reads'\\\\'':\n                       print(req['\\\\''state'\\\\''])\n                       print(req['\\\\''questions'\\\\'']['\\\\''reads__v8'\\\\'']['\\\\''instructions'\\\\''])\n             for qid,answ in ans.items():\n                th=qid.split('\\\\''__'\\\\'')[1]; entry=choices[seq,th]\n                choice,p=(entry['\\\\''reads'\\\\''],entry['\\\\''p'\\\\'']) if j['\\\\''stage'\\\\'']=='\\\\''reads'\\\\'' else (entry['\\\\''sign'\\\\''],entry['\\\\''sp'\\\\''])\n                assert answ['\\\\''choice'\\\\'']==choice and answ['\\\\''probabilities'\\\\'']==p,(qid,jid)\n             item_jobs.append(j['\\\\''stage'\\\\''])\n          for pr in opening['\\\\''proposed'\\\\'']:\n             full=manifest[f'\\\\''{seq}:{pr[\\\"thesis\\\"]}'\\\\'']\n             r,t=pr['\\\\''reader'\\\\''],pr['\\\\''read'\\\\'']\n             r,t=(full['\\\\''new'\\\\''] if x==pr['\\\\''candidate'\\\\''] else x for x in (r,t))\n             assert rc.linked(choices[seq,pr['\\\\''thesis'\\\\'']],full['\\\\''new'\\\\''],pr['\\\\''thesis'\\\\''])==(f'\\\\''{r} reads {t}'\\\\'',pr['\\\\''sign'\\\\''])\n             graph[r].add(t)\n             todo=[t]; visited=set()\n             while todo:\n                cur=todo.pop()\n                assert cur\"'!=r,(list(graph.items()),pr)\n                if cur not in visited:\n                   todo.extend(graph[cur]); visited.add(cur)\n       print(prefix,i,'\"'\\\\''counts'\\\\'',dict(got),'\\\\''jobs'\\\\'',dict(co.Counter(item_jobs)),'\\\\''graph'\\\\'',dict(graph),'\\\\''readers'\\\\'',sorted(k for k,g in graph.items() if g))\nassert tokens==[x['\\\\''tokens'\\\\''] for x in settled[52:]]\nassert all(math.isclose(x['\\\\''charged'\\\\''],3*x['\\\\''tokens'\\\\'']*model.PRICES[cfg.matching.model][0]/1e6) for x in settled)\nprint('\\\\''ledger baseline/v2/total'\\\\'',*[sum(x['\\\\''charged'\\\\''] for x in data) for data in (oldcalls,settled[52:],settled)])\nold=con(wt.OLD2/'\\\\''views.sqlite'\\\\'')\nfor r in old.execute(\\\"select seq, publication_day,rung,reference,implied_outcome from judgements where view_id='\\\\''v8'\\\\'' and publication_day between '\\\\''2026-07-05'\\\\'' and '\\\\''2026-07-12'\\\\'' order by seq\\\"): print('\\\\''v8 judgement:'\\\\'',r)\nfor r in old.execute(\\\"select seq, publication_day,rung,reference,implied_outcome from judgements where view_id='\\\\''v14'\\\\'' and publication_day between '\\\\''2026-07-10'\\\\'' and '\\\\''2026-07-12'\\\\'' order by seq\\\"): print('\\\\''v14 judgement:'\\\\'',r)\nprint('\\\\''v8 and v14 old view'\\\\'',old.execute(\\\"select * from views where view_id in ('\\\\''v8'\\\\'','\\\\''v14'\\\\'')\\\").fetchall())\nprint('\\\\''old successions'\\\\'', old.execute('\\\\''select * from successions'\\\\'').fetchall())\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import collections as co, contextlib, io, json, math, pathlib, sqlite3\nimport read_census as rc\nimport window_test as wt\nfrom hivemind import jev, model\nfrom hivemind.views import links, store, judging\nhere=pathlib.Path.cwd()\nrepo=here.parents[2]\nroot=repo/'\\\\''poc/data/link-census-2026-11-21'\\\\''\ndef con(f): return sqlite3.connect(f.as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro&immutable=1'\\\\'',uri=True)\nledger=json.loads((root/'\\\\''ledger.json'\\\\'').read_text())\nsettled=[json.loads(l) for l in (root/'\\\\''ledger.attempts.jsonl'\\\\'').read_text().splitlines()]\nassert len(settled)==ledger['\\\\''attempts'\\\\'']==103 and all(x['\\\\''kind'\\\\'']=='\\\\''jev'\\\\'' and x['\\\\''charged'\\\\'']<=x['\\\\''reserved'\\\\''] for x in settled)\nassert math.isclose(sum(x['\\\\''charged'\\\\''] for x in settled),ledger['\\\\''spent'\\\\''])\noldcalls=settled[:52]\ntokens=[]\nbaseall=[]\nvarall=[]\nmanifest=json.loads((here/'\\\\''expected-links-v2.json'\\\\'').read_text())\ncfg=wt.config.load(str(wt.V119))\nfor version,prefix,output in [(None,'\\\\''census'\\\\'','\\\\''census-pairs.md'\\\\''),('\\\\''v2'\\\\'','\\\\''probe-v2'\\\\'','\\\\''probe-v2-pairs.md'\\\\'')]:\n dirs=[root/f'\\\\''{prefix}-{i}'\\\\'' for i in range(1,4)]\n capture=io.StringIO()\n with contextlib.redirect_stdout(capture):\n    rc.main((['\\\\''--v2'\\\\''] if version else [])+list(map(str,dirs)))\n assert capture.getvalue()==(here/output).read_text()\n print(output,'\\\\''regenerated identically'\\\\'')\n for i,folder in enumerate(dirs,1):\n    cc=json.loads((folder/'\\\\''census.json'\\\\'').read_text())\n    with con(folder/'\\\\''views.sqlite'\\\\'') as v, con(folder/'\\\\''archive.sqlite'\\\\'') as a:\n       assert cc['\\\\''equal to old-2'\\\\''] and cc['\\\\''link rows written'\\\\'']==0 and wt.complete(cc)==(True,[])\n       assert v.execute('\\\\''select count(*) from dependencies'\\\\'').fetchone()[0]==0\n       choices=rc.decisions(folder/'\\\\''views.sqlite'\\\\'')\n       got=co.Counter()\n       graph=co.defaultdict(set)\n       item_jobs=[]\n       for opening in cc['\\\\''openings with a pair shown'\\\\'']:\n          seq=opening['\\\\''seq'\\\\'']\n          for pair in opening['\\\\''pairs'\\\\'']:\n             th=pair.get('\\\\''thesis'\\\\'')\n             if '\\\\''reads'\\\\'' in pair: got['\\\\''reads'\\\\'']+=1\n             if '\\\\''sign'\\\\'' in pair: got['\\\\''sign'\\\\'']+=1\n          for j in opening['\\\\''calls'\\\\'']:\n             jid,sha=j['\\\\''call_id'\\\\''],j['\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\'']\n             sha2,req_text,reply_text,ans_text,t,created=a.execute('\\\\''select request_sha256,request_json,response_json,answer_json,input_tokens,created_at from model_calls where call_id=?'\\\\'',(jid,)).fetchone()\n             assert j['\\\\''status'\\\\'']=='\\\\''answered'\\\\'' and sha2==sha\n             req=json.loads(req_text); reply=json.loads(reply_text); ans=json.loads(ans_text)\n             assert model.request_identity(req)[1]==sha and sorted(req['\\\\''questions'\\\\''])==j['\\\\''questions'\\\\'']\n             assert jev.validate(ans,req['\\\\''questions'\\\\''])==[] and reply['\\\\''answers'\\\\'']==ans\n             if version=='\\\\''v2'\\\\'':\n                assert j['\\\\''archived_before'\\\\''] is False and reply['\\\\''usage'\\\\'']['\\\\''input_tokens'\\\\'']==t\n                tokens.append(t)\n                rs,sg=wt.wording_v2()\n                for q in req['\\\\''questions'\\\\''].values(): assert q['\\\\''criteria'\\\\'']==(rs if j['\\\\''stage'\\\\'']=='\\\\''reads'\\\\'' else sg)\n                if seq==148:\n                   print(prefix,i,'\\\\''July'\\\\'',j['\\\\''stage'\\\\''],jid,sha[:12],created,t)\n                   if i==1 and j['\\\\''stage'\\\\'']=='\\\\''reads'\\\\'':\n                       print(req['\\\\''state'\\\\''])\n                       print(req['\\\\''questions'\\\\'']['\\\\''reads__v8'\\\\'']['\\\\''instructions'\\\\''])\n             for qid,answ in ans.items():\n                th=qid.split('\\\\''__'\\\\'')[1]; entry=choices[seq,th]\n                choice,p=(entry['\\\\''reads'\\\\''],entry['\\\\''p'\\\\'']) if j['\\\\''stage'\\\\'']=='\\\\''reads'\\\\'' else (entry['\\\\''sign'\\\\''],entry['\\\\''sp'\\\\''])\n                assert answ['\\\\''choice'\\\\'']==choice and answ['\\\\''probabilities'\\\\'']==p,(qid,jid)\n             item_jobs.append(j['\\\\''stage'\\\\''])\n          for pr in opening['\\\\''proposed'\\\\'']:\n             full=manifest[f'\\\\''{seq}:{pr[\\\"thesis\\\"]}'\\\\'']\n             r,t=pr['\\\\''reader'\\\\''],pr['\\\\''read'\\\\'']\n             r,t=(full['\\\\''new'\\\\''] if x==pr['\\\\''candidate'\\\\''] else x for x in (r,t))\n             assert rc.linked(choices[seq,pr['\\\\''thesis'\\\\'']],full['\\\\''new'\\\\''],pr['\\\\''thesis'\\\\''])==(f'\\\\''{r} reads {t}'\\\\'',pr['\\\\''sign'\\\\''])\n             graph[r].add(t)\n             todo=[t]; visited=set()\n             while todo:\n                cur=todo.pop()\n                assert cur\"'!=r,(list(graph.items()),pr)\n                if cur not in visited:\n                   todo.extend(graph[cur]); visited.add(cur)\n       print(prefix,i,'\"'\\\\''counts'\\\\'',dict(got),'\\\\''jobs'\\\\'',dict(co.Counter(item_jobs)),'\\\\''graph'\\\\'',dict(graph),'\\\\''readers'\\\\'',sorted(k for k,g in graph.items() if g))\nassert tokens==[x['\\\\''tokens'\\\\''] for x in settled[52:]]\nassert all(math.isclose(x['\\\\''charged'\\\\''],3*x['\\\\''tokens'\\\\'']*model.PRICES[cfg.matching.model][0]/1e6) for x in settled)\nprint('\\\\''ledger baseline/v2/total'\\\\'',*[sum(x['\\\\''charged'\\\\''] for x in data) for data in (oldcalls,settled[52:],settled)])\nold=con(wt.OLD2/'\\\\''views.sqlite'\\\\'')\nfor r in old.execute(\\\"select seq, publication_day,rung,reference,implied_outcome from judgements where view_id='\\\\''v8'\\\\'' and publication_day between '\\\\''2026-07-05'\\\\'' and '\\\\''2026-07-12'\\\\'' order by seq\\\"): print('\\\\''v8 judgement:'\\\\'',r)\nfor r in old.execute(\\\"select seq, publication_day,rung,reference,implied_outcome from judgements where view_id='\\\\''v14'\\\\'' and publication_day between '\\\\''2026-07-10'\\\\'' and '\\\\''2026-07-12'\\\\'' order by seq\\\"): print('\\\\''v14 judgement:'\\\\'',r)\nprint('\\\\''v8 and v14 old view'\\\\'',old.execute(\\\"select * from views where view_id in ('\\\\''v8'\\\\'','\\\\''v14'\\\\'')\\\").fetchall())\nprint('\\\\''old successions'\\\\'', old.execute('\\\\''select * from successions'\\\\'').fetchall())\n'\"","aggregated_output":"census-pairs.md regenerated identically\ncensus 1 counts {'reads': 105, 'sign': 9} jobs {'reads': 14, 'sign': 6} graph {'v2': {'v1'}, 'v1': set(), 'v9': {'v14'}, 'v14': set(), 'v16': {'v14'}, 'v17': {'v16'}, 'v21': {'v16', 'v9'}, 'v35': {'v14'}} readers ['v16', 'v17', 'v2', 'v21', 'v35', 'v9']\ncensus 2 counts {'reads': 105, 'sign': 9} jobs {'reads': 14, 'sign': 6} graph {'v2': {'v1'}, 'v1': set(), 'v9': {'v21', 'v14'}, 'v14': set(), 'v16': {'v14'}, 'v17': {'v16'}, 'v21': {'v16'}, 'v35': {'v14', 'v9'}} readers ['v16', 'v17', 'v2', 'v21', 'v35', 'v9']\ncensus 3 counts {'reads': 105, 'sign': 6} jobs {'reads': 14, 'sign': 4} graph {'v9': {'v14'}, 'v14': set(), 'v16': {'v14'}, 'v17': {'v16'}, 'v21': {'v16', 'v9'}} readers ['v16', 'v17', 'v21', 'v9']\nprobe-v2-pairs.md regenerated identically\nprobe-v2 1 July reads 8741 b0e2e1c6b281 2026-11-21T09:55:12 3274\nCANDIDATE (asset, object NVDA, focus \"NVIDIA FY2027 total revenue\", FY2027, due 2027-02-28): How much total revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\nKey: measure=total_revenue, period_start=2026-02-01, period_end=2027-01-31, unit=USD\nLadder: Strongly bullish: Total revenue is at least $450 billion. / Bullish: Total revenue is at least $400 billion but less than $450 billion. / Neutral: Total revenue is at least $350 billion but less than $400 billion. / Bearish: Total revenue is at least $300 billion but less than $350 billion. / Strongly bearish: Total revenue is less than $300 billion.\nIts evidence: [Jeran Wittenstein, citing data compiled by Bloomberg ] The chipmaker is projected to deliver $228 billion in profits on sales of $393 billion in fiscal 2027, which ends Jan. 31. That would represent an expansion of 90% and 82%, respectively, according to data compiled by Bloomberg.\nShould one of these two questions be judged with the other's current conclusion in view? Use only the supplied text. THESIS:\nv8 (open, NVDA, asset, focus \"NVIDIA stand-alone CPU sales\", FY2027, due 2027-02-28): How much revenue will NVIDIA generate from stand-alone CPU sales in FY2027?\n    Ladder: Strongly bullish: Stand-alone CPU sales exceed $25 billion in FY2027. / Bullish: Stand-alone CPU sales are at least $20 billion and no more than $25 billion in FY2027. / Neutral: Stand-alone CPU sales are at least $15 billion and less than $20 billion in FY2027. / Bearish: Stand-alone CPU sales are at least $10 billion and less than $15 billion in FY2027. / Strongly bearish: Stand-alone CPU sales are less than $10 billion in FY2027.\n    Evidence: [fool.com (analyst) ] Intel has led here for years and holds more than 59% of total CPU market share\n    Evidence: [fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-05] AMD has gained ground, progressing from a low of about 17% back in 2016 to 38% today.\nprobe-v2 1 July sign 8742 6aa4cab6896d 2026-11-21T09:55:12 1672\nprobe-v2 1 counts {'reads': 105, 'sign': 4} jobs {'reads': 14, 'sign': 3} graph {'v14': {'v8'}, 'v8': set(), 'v9': {'v14'}, 'v16': {'v14'}, 'v21': {'v16'}} readers ['v14', 'v16', 'v21', 'v9']\nprobe-v2 2 July reads 8741 b0e2e1c6b281 2026-11-21T10:01:35 3274\nprobe-v2 2 July sign 8742 6aa4cab6896d 2026-11-21T10:01:35 1672\nprobe-v2 2 counts {'reads': 105, 'sign': 7} jobs {'reads': 14, 'sign': 3} graph {'v14': {'v8'}, 'v8': set(), 'v9': {'v14'}, 'v16': {'v14'}, 'v21': {'v16', 'v9'}} readers ['v14', 'v16', 'v21', 'v9']\nprobe-v2 3 July reads 8741 b0e2e1c6b281 2026-11-21T10:08:00 3274\nprobe-v2 3 July sign 8742 6aa4cab6896d 2026-11-21T10:08:00 1672\nprobe-v2 3 counts {'reads': 105, 'sign': 7} jobs {'reads': 14, 'sign': 3} graph {'v14': {'v8'}, 'v8': set(), 'v9': {'v14'}, 'v16': {'v8', 'v14'}, 'v21': {'v16', 'v9'}} readers ['v14', 'v16', 'v21', 'v9']\nledger baseline/v2/total 0.026553870000000004 0.030945726000000003 0.05749959599999998\nv8 judgement: (51, '2026-07-05', 2, \"NVIDIA's forecast of $20 billion in stand-alone CPU sales for FY2027; this is rung 2.\", \"About $20 billion in FY2027, using NVIDIA's stated forecast directly. The market-share figures for Intel and AMD suggest competitive risk but do not quantify a different NVIDIA revenue outcome.\")\nv8 judgement: (76, '2026-07-06', 2, 'NVIDIA forecasts $20 billion in FY2027 stand-alone CPU sales; this reference sits at rung 2.', 'About $20 billion in FY2027: the stated forecast is the only quantified NVIDIA-specific sales figure, and the competition evidence and capex themes provide no quantified basis to revise it.')\nv8 judgement: (98, '2026-07-07', 2, 'NVIDIA forecasts $20 billion in stand-alone CPU sales in FY2027; this sits at the lower boundary of rung 2.', \"About $20 billion in FY2027, using NVIDIA's stated forecast; the market-share evidence does not quantify a change to that forecast, and the capex themes do not provide a CPU-revenue figure.\")\nv8 judgement: (124, '2026-07-08', 2, 'NVIDIA forecasts $20 billion in FY2027 stand-alone CPU sales; this reference sits at the lower boundary of rung 2.', \"About $20 billion in FY2027, using NVIDIA's stated forecast. The competitive market-share figures do not provide a quantified adjustment to that forecast.\")\nv8 judgement: (167, '2026-07-10', 2, 'NVIDIA’s $20 billion FY2027 stand-alone CPU sales forecast is the available reference and sits at the lower boundary of rung 2; no separate market consensus is supplied.', 'About $20 billion in FY2027, using NVIDIA’s stated forecast as the run-rate/forecast input; the TAM and Perplexity evidence provides no quantified adjustment. That figure is at rung 2’s $20 billion lower boundary.')\nv8 judgement: (186, '2026-07-12', 3, 'NVIDIA’s $20 billion FY2027 stand-alone CPU sales forecast is the supplied reference; it sits at the lower boundary of rung 2.', 'Approximately $18–19 billion in FY2027: an execution-discounted estimate from the $20 billion target because no shipment volume or quantified deployment scale is shown, despite reports of customer interest and offers to cloud customers.')\nv14 judgement: (167, '2026-07-10', 3, 'Bloomberg-compiled projections expect FY2027 sales of $393 billion, which is rung 3 ($350 billion to less than $400 billion).', 'About $393 billion for FY2027, using Bloomberg’s direct sales projection; this is below $400 billion and therefore falls in rung 3.')\nv14 judgement: (172, '2026-07-11', 3, 'Bloomberg-compiled FY2027 sales projection of $393 billion; this market reference sits in rung 3 ($350 billion to less than $400 billion).', \"About $393 billion for FY2027, using Bloomberg's specific projection. The AI-lab demand share and supportive capex and export-policy themes add upside pressure, but state no FY2027 NVIDIA revenue adjustment, so they do not imply a figure above $400 billion.\")\nv14 judgement: (186, '2026-07-12', 3, \"Bloomberg's FY2027 sales projection of $393 billion is the specific market reference and sits in rung 3 ($350 billion to less than $400 billion), $7 billion short of rung 2.\", 'About $387 billion: starting with Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion and Q2 guidance of approximately $91 billion, I carry the roughly 11.5% sequential increase forward to Q3 and Q4. This remains within rung 3 and below $400 billion.')\nv8 and v14 old view [('v14', 'NVDA', 'company', 'asset', 'NVIDIA FY2027 total revenue', 'How much total revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?', '2027-02-28', 'FY2027', 148, 'gnews:49f225cd79fb22132f3b9ee4', '2026-11-17T22:46:26'), ('v8', 'NVDA', 'company', 'asset', 'NVIDIA stand-alone CPU sales', 'How much revenue will NVIDIA generate from stand-alone CPU sales in FY2027?', '2027-02-28', 'FY2027', 49, 'gnews:2f953a56cd06571ab0afc348', '2026-11-17T22:39:50')]\nold successions [(1, 'v33', 'v28', 1102), (2, 'v35', 'v14', 1238)]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"agent_message","text":"All 51 probe calls reconcile to the ledger, and both pair tables regenerate from the archives. The new CPU link is present in all three draws. I’m checking which comparisons can separate its effect on the total from what Data Center does with that total."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba ../2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/rebuild_control.py | sed -n '1,130p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba ../2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/rebuild_control.py | sed -n '1,130p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t\"\"\"$0 step 2 of D694: rebuild old-2's ledger as it stood at the end of 2026-07-09 (the July test's starting state) by replaying the\n     2\tproduct (poc-v118) from 2026-07-01 over old-2's own stored answers. Every request must be answered from the archive: the transport\n     3\trefuses any send, so a request that differs from the stored one by a byte stops the rebuild. The archive is a scratch copy (a\n     4\trefused judge answer is retired in the copy only).\n     5\t\n     6\t  python3 rebuild_control.py <scratch folder>\n     7\t\n     8\tThen it compares the rebuilt ledger with old-2's finished store up to the end of 07-09: views, keys, rungs, evidence, links and\n     9\tjudgements (rung, reasons, request sha) must be equal.\n    10\t\"\"\"\n    11\timport shutil\n    12\timport sqlite3\n    13\timport sys\n    14\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    15\t\n    16\tREPO = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[4]\n    17\tsys.path.insert(0, str(REPO / 'src'))\n    18\tfrom hivemind import config, model, replay, universe        # noqa: E402\n    19\t\n    20\tOLD2 = REPO / 'poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod'\n    21\tITEMS = REPO / 'poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/items-comparison.sqlite'\n    22\tUNTIL = '2026-07-09'\n    23\t\n    24\t\n    25\tclass SendRefused(RuntimeError):\n    26\t    pass\n    27\t\n    28\t\n    29\tdef refuse(*args, **kwargs):\n    30\t    raise SendRefused('a request was not in the archive: the rebuilt request differs from the stored one')\n    31\t\n    32\t\n    33\tdef rows(conn, sql, args=()):\n    34\t    return [tuple(r) for r in conn.execute(sql, args)]\n    35\t\n    36\t\n    37\tdef compare(rebuilt_path, last_seq):\n    38\t    rebuilt = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{rebuilt_path}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    39\t    stored = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{OLD2}/views.sqlite?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    40\t    checks = {\n    41\t        'views': ('select view_id, question, created_seq from views where created_seq <= ? order by view_id', (last_seq,)),\n    42\t        'view_keys': ('select view_id, measure, scope, period_start, period_end, unit from view_keys where seq <= ? order by view_id', (last_seq,)),\n    43\t        'evidence': ('select evidence_id, quote, created_seq from evidence where created_seq <= ? order by evidence_id', (last_seq,)),\n    44\t        'evidence_links': ('select evidence_id, view_id, seq from evidence_links where seq <= ? order by evidence_id, view_id', (last_seq,)),\n    45\t        'judgements': ('select view_id, seq, rung, reasons, cited_evidence_json, cited_views_json, changed, reference, implied_outcome, request_sha256 from judgements where seq <= ? order by judgement_id', (last_seq,)),\n    46\t        'rungs': ('select r.view_id, r.position, r.label, r.condition, r.lo, r.hi from rungs r join views v using(view_id) where v.created_seq <= ? order by r.view_id, r.position', (last_seq,)),\n    47\t        'view_switches': ('select view_id, open, reason, after_seq from view_switches where after_seq <= ? order by id', (last_seq,)),\n    48\t        'successions': ('select view_id, succeeds, seq from successions where seq <= ? order by id', (last_seq,)),\n    49\t        'dependencies': ('select view_id, depends_on, seq from dependencies where seq <= ? order by dependency_id', (last_seq,)),\n    50\t    }\n    51\t    ok = True\n    52\t    for name, (sql, args) in checks.items():\n    53\t        a, b = rows(rebuilt, sql, args), rows(stored, sql, args)\n    54\t        same = a == b\n    55\t        ok = ok and same\n    56\t        print(f'{name}: rebuilt {len(a)} stored {len(b)} {\"equal\" if same else \"DIFFER\"}')\n    57\t        if not same:\n    58\t            for x, y in zip(a, b):\n    59\t                if x != y:\n    60\t                    print('  first difference:', str(x)[:200], '|', str(y)[:200])\n    61\t                    break\n    62\t    return ok\n    63\t\n    64\t\n    65\tdef main():\n    66\t    scratch = Path(sys.argv[1])\n    67\t    scratch.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    68\t    views_path, archive_path = scratch / 'views.sqlite', scratch / 'archive.sqlite'\n    69\t    for path in (views_path, archive_path):\n    70\t        if path.exists():\n    71\t            raise SystemExit(f'{path} exists: a rebuild starts from an empty folder')\n    72\t    shutil.copyfile(OLD2 / 'archive.sqlite', archive_path)\n    73\t    cfg = config.load(str(REPO / 'poc/config/poc-v118.json'))\n    74\t    uni = universe.load(str(REPO / 'poc/universe.json'))\n    75\t    totals = replay.run(testdb_path=str(ITEMS), views_path=str(views_path), archive=model.Archive(str(archive_path)), cfg=cfg,\n    76\t                        universe=uni, from_day='2026-07-01', until_day=UNTIL, transport=refuse, log=print,\n    77\t                        only_objects={'NVDA'})          # the comparison launcher's default (`budget_replay.py --only NVDA`)\n    78\t    print('totals:', totals)\n    79\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{views_path}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    80\t    last_seq = conn.execute('select max(seq) from days_completed where day=?', (UNTIL,)).fetchone()[0]\n    81\t    print('last completed seq at', UNTIL, last_seq)\n    82\t    sys.exit(0 if compare(views_path, last_seq) else 1)\n    83\t\n    84\t\n    85\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n    86\t    main()\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'def compare|def projection|def rows|sqlite3.connect' ../2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/rebuild_control.py; nl -ba ../../../poc/data/link-census-2026-11-21/probe-v2-1/census.json | sed -n '385,510p'; nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/views/store.py | sed -n '227,245p'; nl -ba probe-v2-pairs.md | tail -9; nl -ba ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md | tail -23\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'def compare|def projection|def rows|sqlite3.connect' ../2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/rebuild_control.py; nl -ba ../../../poc/data/link-census-2026-11-21/probe-v2-1/census.json | sed -n '385,510p'; nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/views/store.py | sed -n '227,245p'; nl -ba probe-v2-pairs.md | tail -9; nl -ba ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md | tail -23\"","aggregated_output":"33:def rows(conn, sql, args=()):\n37:def compare(rebuilt_path, last_seq):\n38:    rebuilt = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{rebuilt_path}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n39:    stored = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{OLD2}/views.sqlite?mode=ro', uri=True)\n79:    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{views_path}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n   385\t     \"candidate\": \"c1\",\n   386\t     \"eligible\": false,\n   387\t     \"thesis\": \"v11\"\n   388\t    },\n   389\t    {\n   390\t     \"candidate\": \"c1\",\n   391\t     \"eligible\": false,\n   392\t     \"thesis\": \"v13\"\n   393\t    },\n   394\t    {\n   395\t     \"candidate\": \"c1\",\n   396\t     \"probabilities\": {\n   397\t      \"candidate_reads_thesis\": 0.48,\n   398\t      \"neither\": 0.01,\n   399\t      \"thesis_reads_candidate\": 0.51\n   400\t     },\n   401\t     \"reads\": \"thesis_reads_candidate\",\n   402\t     \"thesis\": \"v9\"\n   403\t    },\n   404\t    {\n   405\t     \"candidate\": \"c1\",\n   406\t     \"probabilities\": {\n   407\t      \"candidate_reads_thesis\": 0.53,\n   408\t      \"neither\": 0.1,\n   409\t      \"thesis_reads_candidate\": 0.37\n   410\t     },\n   411\t     \"reads\": \"candidate_reads_thesis\",\n   412\t     \"thesis\": \"v8\"\n   413\t    },\n   414\t    {\n   415\t     \"candidate\": \"c1\",\n   416\t     \"probabilities\": {\n   417\t      \"candidate_reads_thesis\": 0.11,\n   418\t      \"neither\": 0.53,\n   419\t      \"thesis_reads_candidate\": 0.36\n   420\t     },\n   421\t     \"reads\": \"neither\",\n   422\t     \"thesis\": \"v1\"\n   423\t    },\n   424\t    {\n   425\t     \"candidate\": \"c1\",\n   426\t     \"probabilities\": {\n   427\t      \"candidate_reads_thesis\": 0.15,\n   428\t      \"neither\": 0.49,\n   429\t      \"thesis_reads_candidate\": 0.36\n   430\t     },\n   431\t     \"reads\": \"neither\",\n   432\t     \"thesis\": \"v2\"\n   433\t    },\n   434\t    {\n   435\t     \"candidate\": \"c1\",\n   436\t     \"probabilities\": {\n   437\t      \"no_clear_sign\": 0.4,\n   438\t      \"opposite\": 0.01,\n   439\t      \"together\": 0.59\n   440\t     },\n   441\t     \"sign\": \"together\",\n   442\t     \"thesis\": \"v8\"\n   443\t    },\n   444\t    {\n   445\t     \"candidate\": \"c1\",\n   446\t     \"probabilities\": {\n   447\t      \"no_clear_sign\": 0.07,\n   448\t      \"opposite\": 0.0,\n   449\t      \"together\": 0.93\n   450\t     },\n   451\t     \"sign\": \"together\",\n   452\t     \"thesis\": \"v9\"\n   453\t    }\n   454\t   ],\n   455\t   \"calls\": [\n   456\t    {\n   457\t     \"archived_before\": false,\n   458\t     \"call_id\": 8741,\n   459\t     \"questions\": [\n   460\t      \"reads__v1\",\n   461\t      \"reads__v2\",\n   462\t      \"reads__v8\",\n   463\t      \"reads__v9\"\n   464\t     ],\n   465\t     \"request_sha256\": \"b0e2e1c6b281d56fa96ec44a55142b0556872b4c9e4cfc5332d7dd8f98e5c22a\",\n   466\t     \"stage\": \"reads\",\n   467\t     \"status\": \"answered\"\n   468\t    },\n   469\t    {\n   470\t     \"archived_before\": false,\n   471\t     \"call_id\": 8742,\n   472\t     \"questions\": [\n   473\t      \"sign__v8\",\n   474\t      \"sign__v9\"\n   475\t     ],\n   476\t     \"request_sha256\": \"6aa4cab6896dbe282d10c0360cb77e64da2ed81dea89758ee7eec8caa3c1bf76\",\n   477\t     \"stage\": \"sign\",\n   478\t     \"status\": \"answered\"\n   479\t    }\n   480\t   ],\n   481\t   \"proposed\": [\n   482\t    {\n   483\t     \"candidate\": \"c1\",\n   484\t     \"direction\": \"candidate_reads_thesis\",\n   485\t     \"read\": \"v8\",\n   486\t     \"reader\": \"c1\",\n   487\t     \"sign\": \"together\",\n   488\t     \"thesis\": \"v8\"\n   489\t    },\n   490\t    {\n   491\t     \"candidate\": \"c1\",\n   492\t     \"direction\": \"thesis_reads_candidate\",\n   493\t     \"read\": \"c1\",\n   494\t     \"reader\": \"v9\",\n   495\t     \"sign\": \"together\",\n   496\t     \"thesis\": \"v9\"\n   497\t    }\n   498\t   ],\n   499\t   \"corrections\": []\n   500\t  },\n   501\t  {\n   502\t   \"attempt\": \"gnews:221f52333c8f5e936e515c4d#1\",\n   503\t   \"seq\": 206,\n   504\t   \"pairs\": [\n   505\t    {\n   506\t     \"candidate\": \"c1\",\n   507\t     \"eligible\": true,\n   508\t     \"thesis\": \"v1\"\n   509\t    },\n   510\t    {\n   227\t    from hivemind import live_lock\n   228\t    real, _ = live_lock.own_path(path)\n   229\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{real}?mode=ro', uri=True, timeout=READ_BUSY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS)\n   230\t    conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\n   231\t    return conn\n   232\t\n   233\t\n   234\tdef current_state(conn, view_id):\n   235\t    \"\"\"The latest judgement: rung, reasons, changed, seq and day, and its reference and implied outcome (D260) where the ledger has them.\"\"\"\n   236\t    columns = {r[1] for r in conn.execute('pragma table_info(judgements)')}\n   237\t    stance = ''.join(f', {field}' for field in ('reference', 'implied_outcome') if field in columns)\n   238\t    row = conn.execute(f'select judgement_id, rung, reasons, changed, seq, publication_day{stance} from judgements where view_id=? order by judgement_id desc limit 1', (view_id,)).fetchone()\n   239\t    return dict(row) if row else None\n   240\t\n   241\t\n   242\tdef dependencies_of(conn, view_id):\n   243\t    \"\"\"Each dependency with its current target: the resolved view, or the waiting chain and year.\"\"\"\n   244\t    out = []\n   245\t    for dep in conn.execute('select * from dependencies where view_id=? order by dependency_id', (view_id,)):\n   108\t| 1262 | v36 | v33 | W |  | none 0.91 (m 0.86) → right | none 0.94 (m 0.91) → right | none 0.92 (m 0.87) → right |\n   109\t| 1262 | v36 | v35 | W |  | none 0.88 (m 0.81) → right | none 0.89 (m 0.83) → right | none 0.91 (m 0.86) → right |\n   110\t\n   111\tDraws: 3 (version 2: every link job asked fresh, the seq-148 jobs included).\n   112\tKnown positive right: 3; missed: 0 []\n   113\tWrong links: 0 []\n   114\tFragile (margin below 0.10 on a linked or required pair): 2 [('probe-v2-1', '148:v9', 0.03), ('probe-v2-2', '148:v9', 0.07)]\n   115\t\n   116\tGate (no wrong link in any draw; the known positive right in every draw): PASS\n 10559\t  Options: 先试新问法 (recommended: with Codex at $0, write the link question clearly, keeping Data Center reads total revenue and the\n 10560\t  38 negatives, removing unsupported links including the base effect, no blanket ban on a whole reading its part; then ask the same\n 10561\t  105 pairs three times, about 3 cents, from the 7 cents left of the approved 10; then decide the paid run); 直接正式运行 (the current\n 10562\t  wording, about $7 estimated, ceiling later); 停在这里 (poc-v118 stays, the linking version paused).\n 10563\t- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-21): \"先试新问法 (推荐)\".\n 10564\t- **Decided (Alex):** a sharpened READS/SIGN wording is designed with the council at $0 and probed on the same 105 pairs, three draws,\n 10565\t  within the remaining $0.073 of D700's ledger. Then the paid run is decided.\n 10566\t\n 10567\t## D704 · 2026-11-21 · Council R passes the version-2 link question for its probe (rounds 18–19); the probe is sent under D703\n 10568\t\n 10569\t- **The wording** (`docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/WORDING-V2.md`, harness-only, no product file changed): a tie-break (when\n 10570\t  either question could read the other, the one less anchored by guidance, consensus or a reported figure for the quantity and full\n 10571\t  period it asks about reads the other; no direction banned); a periods clause (quantities of different periods are linked only when\n 10572\t  the supplied text states how one moves the other); a base-effect SIGN example. The tie-break and the periods clause are proposals\n 10573\t  this probe tests under D703; D537 decided only the Data Center case.\n 10574\t- **The council:** round 18 NOT READY (the gate could pass while keeping an unsupported cross-period link; the tie-break's period and\n 10575\t  the periods example needed precision); round 19 READY FOR THE V2 PROBE. Registration for version 2, written before its answers: R 1,\n 10576\t  W 40 (the census's 38 plus 321:v16 and 1238:v9, no bridge across periods), O 61, F 3 (a growth rate reading an earlier revenue amount\n 10577\t  with the sign together). $0: the dry pass complete and equal to old-2 with every job carrying the version-2 texts; its mutant (texts\n 10578\t  not patched) stops before any send; the stored census answers fail the version-2 gate, the round-18 counterexample fails it, a\n 10579\t  control with both unsupported links removed passes.\n 10580\t- **Sent:** `window_test.py probe-v2`, draws 1, 2, 3 one after another on D700's ledger ($0.0734 left); a ceiling stop before draw 3\n 10581\t  is an incomplete probe with no verdict.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import contextlib, io, pathlib, sqlite3\nimport window_test as w\nroot=w.REPO/'\\\\''poc/data/link-census-2026-11-21'\\\\''\nfor i in range(1,4):\n p=root/f'\\\\''probe-v2-{i}'\\\\''/'\\\\''views.sqlite'\\\\''\n con=sqlite3.connect(p.as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro&immutable=1'\\\\'',uri=True)\n assert con.execute('\\\\''select max(seq) from days_completed'\\\\'').fetchone()[0]==1884\n sink=io.StringIO()\n with contextlib.redirect_stdout(sink): assert w.rebuild_control.compare(p,1884)\n print(i,len(sink.getvalue().splitlines()),'\\\\''stored projections equal'\\\\'')\np=w.OLD2/'\\\\''views.sqlite'\\\\''\ncon=sqlite3.connect(p.as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro&immutable=1'\\\\'',uri=True)\nfor row in con.execute(\\\"select view_id, count(*), min(seq), max(seq),min(publication_day),max(publication_day) from judgements where view_id in ('\\\\''v8'\\\\'','\\\\''v9'\\\\'','\\\\''v14'\\\\'','\\\\''v16'\\\\'','\\\\''v21'\\\\'') and seq>=148 group by view_id\\\"): print(row)\nfor row in con.execute(\\\"select v.view_id,v.created_seq,s.open,s.reason,s.after_seq from views v left join view_switches s using(view_id) where view_id in ('\\\\''v8'\\\\'','\\\\''v9'\\\\'','\\\\''v14'\\\\'','\\\\''v16'\\\\'','\\\\''v21'\\\\'') order by created_seq\\\"): print(row)'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import contextlib, io, pathlib, sqlite3\nimport window_test as w\nroot=w.REPO/'\\\\''poc/data/link-census-2026-11-21'\\\\''\nfor i in range(1,4):\n p=root/f'\\\\''probe-v2-{i}'\\\\''/'\\\\''views.sqlite'\\\\''\n con=sqlite3.connect(p.as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro&immutable=1'\\\\'',uri=True)\n assert con.execute('\\\\''select max(seq) from days_completed'\\\\'').fetchone()[0]==1884\n sink=io.StringIO()\n with contextlib.redirect_stdout(sink): assert w.rebuild_control.compare(p,1884)\n print(i,len(sink.getvalue().splitlines()),'\\\\''stored projections equal'\\\\'')\np=w.OLD2/'\\\\''views.sqlite'\\\\''\ncon=sqlite3.connect(p.as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro&immutable=1'\\\\'',uri=True)\nfor row in con.execute(\\\"select view_id, count(*), min(seq), max(seq),min(publication_day),max(publication_day) from judgements where view_id in ('\\\\''v8'\\\\'','\\\\''v9'\\\\'','\\\\''v14'\\\\'','\\\\''v16'\\\\'','\\\\''v21'\\\\'') and seq>=148 group by view_id\\\"): print(row)\nfor row in con.execute(\\\"select v.view_id,v.created_seq,s.open,s.reason,s.after_seq from views v left join view_switches s using(view_id) where view_id in ('\\\\''v8'\\\\'','\\\\''v9'\\\\'','\\\\''v14'\\\\'','\\\\''v16'\\\\'','\\\\''v21'\\\\'') order by created_seq\\\"): print(row)'\"","aggregated_output":"1 9 stored projections equal\n2 9 stored projections equal\n3 9 stored projections equal\n('v14', 71, 167, 1884, '2026-07-10', '2026-09-20')\n('v16', 56, 274, 1884, '2026-07-15', '2026-09-20')\n('v21', 50, 542, 1884, '2026-07-26', '2026-09-20')\n('v8', 62, 167, 1884, '2026-07-10', '2026-09-20')\n('v9', 70, 167, 1884, '2026-07-10', '2026-09-20')\n('v8', 49, 1, 'created', 49)\n('v9', 62, 1, 'created', 62)\n('v14', 148, 1, 'created', 148)\n('v16', 265, 1, 'created', 265)\n('v21', 534, 1, 'created', 534)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"agent_message","text":"**TAKE VERSION 2 TO THE PAID DESIGN.** The registered PASS holds. Version 2 kept the Data Center link in all three draws and dropped both unsupported cross-period links. It also added a weak link in all three draws: total revenue reads stand-alone CPU sales. The paid design should keep that link and measure what it does to the total before crediting any improvement in Data Center. [Probe results](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PROBE-V2-RESULT.md:7)\n\n### 1. The PASS is sound\n\nI regenerated both 105-pair tables from the stored draws and matched them to the published tables. Each V2 draw completed 105 READS decisions. All 51 jobs, including the July jobs, carried the revised wording, missed the copied archive, and reconciled to the ledger. Each draw matched old-2 on all nine compared store projections through seq 1884 and wrote zero links. The known positive was right **3/3**, with **zero forbidden links across 120 W and nine F decisions**. The probe settled **$0.030945726**, bringing total ledger spend to **$0.057499596** of $0.10, with no refusal or overrun. I found no invalid draw. [Registered rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/WORDING-V2.md:43) · [Pair table](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/probe-v2-pairs.md:111) · [Store comparison](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/rebuild_control.py:37) · [Ledger](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/link-census-2026-11-21/ledger.json:2)\n\n### 2. The new July link is weak\n\nI agree with Claude’s inventory. The two unsupported links disappeared, two defensible links disappeared, and the `v21–v9` reversal did not recur. The known positive still had a margin below 0.10 in two draws. One qualification: the probe changed three pieces of wording together. The results establish which links changed, while the effect of each sentence remains unmeasured. For the defensible `v35 reads v14` link, two V2 draws still favoured that direction below the threshold. [Claude’s read](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/claude-r20.md:3) · [Current-wording table](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/census-pairs.md:20) · [V2 table](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/probe-v2-pairs.md:84)\n\n**`v14 reads v8` is weak, with plausible downstream harm.** The seq-148 request gave the total a direct **$393B FY2027** estimate. The CPU card showed its ladder and Intel and AMD market shares. It supplied no full-year NVIDIA CPU forecast in the evidence shown to the matcher. If both directions would help, the tie-break favours the CPU question reading the total. The broad total also gives the CPU question little useful constraint, so `neither` is defensible. The positive sign is arithmetically plausible if other sales hold fixed. The risk is that the total treats an uncertain CPU forecast as incremental to a company estimate that may already include those sales. The probe bought no judgements, so that harm remains unmeasured. [Seq-148 request record, archive call 8741](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/link-census-2026-11-21/probe-v2-1/census.json:455) · [Evidence shown to the matcher](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py:56) · [Tie-break](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/WORDING-V2.md:16)\n\n### 3. One next step\n\n**Choose (a).** Put the tested wording into a separately versioned, reviewed product configuration, then design the paid comparison. A third wording could improve the CPU decision or recover the two lost links. Choosing it by performance on these same 105 pairs would be selection on the probe set, so those pairs could diagnose the change but could no longer independently validate that choice. Returning to the current wording avoids the new CPU link and keeps the two defensible links, while bringing back the known base-effect error. Stopping saves the judgement spend and leaves the product question unanswered. The eventual send still needs the design pass and Alex’s ceiling. [Registered next step](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/WORDING-V2.md:53) · [Iteration rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/AGENTS.md:326) · [D699](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10505)\n\n### 4. Keep the full chain and read it one step at a time\n\nIn each linked sequence, commit both seq-148 links. First prove at $0 that the product version reproduces its paired probe request hashes and graph. Replay `v8` by exact request identity wherever its inputs are unchanged. Let production judge `v14` before `v9` when both are due. In each paired no-link control, sample both `v14` and `v9` fresh from their first affected judgement onward, without forcing extra control judgement days. [Paired control design](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/DESIGN.md:153) · [Judgement order](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:305)\n\nFor each common date, show **which CPU conclusion the linked total saw, how that total compares with its fresh control, and which exact total Data Center saw**. Judge Data Center against its own sequence’s available total. Report days added by propagation separately. Credit reconciliation only when the forecasts still have sound arithmetic and sourcing. Moving the whole to accommodate the part would be visible in the `v14` comparison. This measures the full V2 chain. The original July test remains the separate evidence for the single Data Center link. [Dependency block](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:127) · [Propagation](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:350) · [July reading rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/reading-rule.md:5)"}}
